## ⚙️ Setup Instructions

### Prerequisites
- AWS Account with EC2, S3, Athena access
- Ubuntu EC2 instance (c7i.flex.large recommended)
- Python 3.x
- Java 11

### Step 1 — Clone Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/railway-pipeline.git
cd railway-pipeline
```

### Step 2 — EC2 Setup
```bash
# Update machine
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install Java
sudo apt install -y openjdk-11-jdk

# Install Kafka
wget https://archive.apache.org/dist/kafka/3.7.0/kafka_2.13-3.7.0.tgz
tar -xzf kafka_2.13-3.7.0.tgz
sudo mv kafka_2.13-3.7.0 /opt/kafka
echo 'export KAFKA_HOME=/opt/kafka' >> ~/.bashrc
echo 'export PATH=$PATH:$KAFKA_HOME/bin' >> ~/.bashrc

# Install Spark
wget https://archive.apache.org/dist/spark/spark-3.5.0/spark-3.5.0-bin-hadoop3.tgz
tar -xzf spark-3.5.0-bin-hadoop3.tgz
sudo mv spark-3.5.0-bin-hadoop3 /opt/spark
echo 'export SPARK_HOME=/opt/spark' >> ~/.bashrc
echo 'export PYSPARK_PYTHON=python3' >> ~/.bashrc
echo 'export PYTHONPATH=/opt/spark/python:/opt/spark/python/lib/py4j-0.10.9.7-src.zip' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

# Install Python libraries
pip3 install -r requirements.txt --break-system-packages

# Install AWS CLI
sudo apt install -y awscli
```

### Step 3 — Configure AWS Credentials
```bash
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<YOUR_ACCESS_KEY>
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<YOUR_SECRET_KEY>
export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
```

### Step 4 — Start Kafka
```bash
# Start Zookeeper
$KAFKA_HOME/bin/zookeeper-server-start.sh $KAFKA_HOME/config/zookeeper.properties &
sleep 10

# Start Kafka
$KAFKA_HOME/bin/kafka-server-start.sh $KAFKA_HOME/config/server.properties &
sleep 10

# Verify
jps  # Should show QuorumPeerMain + Kafka
```

### Step 5 — Create Kafka Topics
```bash
$KAFKA_HOME/bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --replication-factor 1 --partitions 1 --topic trains_topic
$KAFKA_HOME/bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --replication-factor 1 --partitions 1 --topic stations_topic
$KAFKA_HOME/bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --replication-factor 1 --partitions 1 --topic schedules_topic
```

### Step 6 — Run Pipeline
```bash
# Run Producer
python3 producer/producer.py

# Run Consumer
python3 consumer/consumer.py
```

### Step 7 — Airflow (Optional)
```bash
airflow db migrate
airflow users create --username admin --password admin123 --role Admin --firstname admin --lastname admin --email admin@example.com
airflow standalone &
```

